   "text": "I read the structure as a Tris-core triantennary GalNAc conjugate of a 16-residue disulfide-bridged peptide. I could not confirm each stereocentre from the wedges and hashes, so I assigned L-amino acids and \u03b2-D-GalNAc by default.\n\n**Peptide.** Reading from the N-terminus, the sequence is His-Gln-Val-Cys-Leu-Ser-Tyr-Arg-Gly-Arg-Pro-Val-Cys-Phe-Ser-Thr-NH2. The two Cys residues are joined by a disulfide bond, and the C-terminus is a primary amide.\n\n**Linker.** The His amine is acylated by C(=O)CH2-O-CH2CH2-O-CH2CH2-O-CH2-C(=O)-NH-, which leads into a quaternary carbon.\n\n**Branches.** The quaternary carbon carries three identical arms: CH2-O-CH2CH2-C(=O)-NH-CH2CH2-(OCH2CH2)3-O-CH2-, each ending at C6 of a sugar.\n\n**Sugar.** Each sugar is a methyl 2-acetamido-2-deoxy-\u03b2-D-galactopyranoside (\u03b2-D-GalNAc) joined through its 6-O.\n\nI checked the SMILES for valid ring closures, the disulfide closure, and the arm and peptide connectivity against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: C(COCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOC[C@H]1O[C@@H](OC)[C@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](O)[C@H]1O)(COCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOC[C@H]2O[C@@H](OC)[C@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](O)[C@H]2O)(COCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOC[C@H]3O[C@@H](OC)[C@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](O)[C@H]3O)NC(=O)COCCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc4c[nH]cn4)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc4ccc(O)cc4)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc6ccccc6)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(N)=O"
